msgid "The building blocks every pattern is made from. Each item is labeled with the class or token you type to use it."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:30
msgid "Colors"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:30
msgid "Role tokens, applied as <code>has-{slug}-color</code> for text or <code>has-{slug}-background-color</code> for a fill. Every value is adaptive - it follows the visitor&#8217;s light or dark setting."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:90
msgid "Brand ramp - the accessible tonal scale derived from your brand color (<code>primary-50</code> to <code>primary-950</code>). <code>primary</code> itself is the scheme&#8217;s brand color."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:94
msgid "Neutral ramp - surfaces, text, and borders derive from this scale."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:98
msgid "Semantic status colors - each has a full 50-950 ramp; the 500 is shown."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:115
msgid "Typography"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:115
msgid "Font sizes, applied as <code>has-{slug}-font-size</code>. Each line is set at the size it names."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:115
msgid "Font families, applied as <code>has-{slug}-font-family</code>."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:116
msgid "Buttons"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:116
msgid "Four emphasis tiers, strongest to quietest. Use one primary (Fill) per view and let the rest recede. All adapt to the color variation and to light/dark, and meet WCAG AA. The Styles panel labels these Fill / Soft / Outline / Subtle."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:127
msgid "Fill, the one main action"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:142
msgid "Soft, secondary emphasis"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:157
msgid "Outline, quiet secondary"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:172
msgid "Subtle, lowest emphasis"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:177
msgid "Links"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:177
msgid "The <code>a</code> element. Inline links use the link color with an underline."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:177
msgid "A paragraph with an <a href=\"#elements\">inline link</a> and following text, so it can be seen in running copy."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:178
msgid "Editorial roles"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:178
msgid "Brand-colored text styles for labels and notes. Each carries the scheme hue through tokens, so it re-hues with the color variation and meets WCAG AA in light and dark. The Styles panel labels these Eyebrow / Badge, plus a Callout group style."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:179
msgid "Eyebrow above a heading"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:180
msgid "New"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:181
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/style-guide-content.php:181
